#X obj 638 8 flow.multiplex;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 270 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Passes messages from one of several inlets to a single
outlet \, according to the current input index. The number of inlets
is set by the argument N. Only one inlet at a time is routed to the
outlet — the others are ignored.;
#X text 240 168 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 193 • Selecting one of several control sources — choosing
between different sliders \, knobs or MIDI inputs \, so that only the
currently selected source updates the parameter.;
#X text 250 263 • Programmatic switching in algorithmic patches — changing
the active input on the fly from a sequencer \, LFO or any other control
signal \, so that the flow of messages is redirected automatically.;
